  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "A Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is a product development strategy featuring only essential, core functionality to satisfy early adopters and validate ideas with minimum expenditure. By launching a functional, bare-bones solution, businesses test market demand, reduce innovation risks, and gain crucial feedback to inform future development phases. Key aspects of an MVP include: Purpose: To maximize learning about the customer while minimizing risk and capital. Testing & Feedback: Validating whether the product solves a specific problem or if the concept is viable. Iteration: Using initial feedback to iteratively improve the product. AI Context: AI MVPs use intelligent features like machine learning or natural language processing as a core component of the user experience, often differentiating them from traditional MVPs. Other common uses of \"MVP\": Sports: Most Valuable Player (e.g., NBA MVP). Business: Most Valuable Promotions, a boxing and MMA promotion company. Health: MVP Health Care or the Million Veteran Program (VA research program). Tech: Model–view–presenter (software architectural pattern).",
